  This OSK port has been made using the PD Korn shell.  For yourconvenience, I have added the PostScript translation of the manual (ed.ps)and a short file with questions and answers about ed (ed.quiz) extractedfrom the Unix quiz program.  The following assumptions have been made when doing the port:1. The temporary files are stored on the RAM disk.  There should be enough   space there to store the edited files.  If you do not like this   assumption, change the string "/r0/ed.XXXXXX" in file buf.c and recompile   or patch the binaries.2. In the original version error reporting is different if the ed input is   interactive (see the manual for the exact definition).  In the OSK port   the input is defined to be interactive if it comes from an SCF device.   This is done in file "main.c" in function "is_regular_file".  I did not include in this archive the TESTSUITE directory which contains aseries of tests.  However, I made sure that the OSK version passes them.  Enjoy,  Andrzej Kotanski(kotanski@if.uj.edu.pl or kotanski@desy.de)                                                      Cracow, March 25, 1996. 